              <h2 class="story-title">Project Overview</h2>
              <div class="story-text">
                <p style="font-size:1.125rem;">Square was already the point of sale at farmers markets. So the design started from a constraint rather than a feature list: Square stays authoritative, and the website is a view onto it — never a second ledger to reconcile.</p>
                <p style="margin-top:1rem;">That ruled out the conventional answers. A standard platform would want to own the catalog and the stock count, leaving two systems to keep in step. Instead we built a storefront that holds no commerce data of its own.</p>
              </div>
