            <h2>What We Delivered</h2>
            <p>One inventory, two sales channels, no reconciling</p>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-3 stagger-children">
            <div class="card">
              <div class="icon-box icon-box-primary" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;"><i data-lucide="refresh-cw"></i></div>
              <h3 class="card-title">Live Catalog from Square</h3>
              <p class="card-desc">Products, prices, images and stock all come from Square, with caching so the shop stays fast. Add a product in Square and it appears online; sell one at a market and the count drops.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="icon-box icon-box-primary" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;"><i data-lucide="shield-check"></i></div>
              <h3 class="card-title">Stock-Aware Checkout</h3>
              <p class="card-desc">The cart won't exceed available stock, and quantities are re-validated against live inventory before checkout is created. Carts left open for a week can't carry quantities that no longer exist.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="icon-box icon-box-primary" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;"><i data-lucide="package"></i></div>
              <h3 class="card-title">Shipping or Local Pickup</h3>
              <p class="card-desc">Modelled as distinct Square fulfillments rather than a shipping line item — so pickup orders simply never ask for a shipping address.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Challenge & Solution -->
      <section class="section section-light">
        <div class="container" style="max-width:56rem;">
          <div class="fade-in">
            <div class="challenge-solution" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:3rem;">
              <div>
                <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-weight:700;font-size:1.5rem;color:var(--primary);margin-bottom:1rem;">
                  <i data-lucide="alert-circle" style="color:var(--accent);width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;display:inline;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:0.5rem;"></i>
                  The Challenge
                </h3>
                <p style="color:var(--muted-foreground);line-height:1.7;font-weight:300;">Selling the same handmade stock in two places at once. Every conventional store platform wants to own the inventory, which for a maker already running Square at markets means two counts, two places to update, and eventually an oversold order.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-weight:700;font-size:1.5rem;color:var(--primary);margin-bottom:1rem;">
                  <i data-lucide="lightbulb" style="color:var(--accent);width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;display:inline;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:0.5rem;"></i>
                  Our Solution
                </h3>
                <p style="color:var(--muted-foreground);line-height:1.7;font-weight:300;">Make Square the single source of truth and give the website no inventory of its own. Sign-in runs through Square itself, so there's no extra password to manage — and a one-time recovery key handles the thing that actually happens eventually: lost access.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

